## Business Type

{{Is this a service-area business (travels to customers, no single
storefront) or a fixed-location business? This changes the whole
strategy:}}
- Service-area: proximity to searcher is fixed and can't be controlled —
  relevance and prominence CAN be built, that's where the work goes. Must
  win far-town visibility through the website itself, since the map pack
  naturally favors towns near the home base.
- Fixed-location: proximity IS controllable somewhat (the address itself),
  different playbook.

## The Two Levers

- **Organic (website)** — one page per service × area combination, each
  genuinely unique, not thin
- **Map pack (Google Business Profile)** — once a real GBP exists,
  service area + categories must mirror the website's service pages
  exactly

## Search Intent → Page Type Mapping

| Intent | Example | Page type |
|---|---|---|
| Informational | "how often should X be replaced" | Blog / FAQ post |
| Commercial | "X cost [region]" | Service hub page |
| Local-transactional | "emergency X [town]" | Area page |
| Navigational | "{{business name}}" | Homepage |

